LATEST IMPLEMENTATION — MB-03A
mirror_storage::v2 exposes StoreV2, StoreAccessV2, StorageErrorV2 and SelectionRecordV2.
StoreV2::initialize(path, &accepted_chain) accepts an absent final directory under an
existing parent or an explicitly empty directory. It persists a full already accepted
finite ChainV2, including genesis-only histories. It never mines, imports a state cache,
creates missing parents, migrates legacy data, grants funds or trusts a peer's network.
StoreV2::open_writer(path, identity, expected) and inspect(path, identity, expected)
require independent ManifestIdentityV2(C, genesis) and ChainReplayExpectationV2
(C, genesis, height, tip, ledger_root). These arguments must agree before I/O.
Never derive them from the untrusted input being checked. They select a finite
branch; they do not establish global freshness.

Returned handles own an immutable accepted chain and retain their Linux root-directory
inode lock for life. Writer mode is exclusive; inspection is shared. Multiple inspectors
coexist and exclude a writer. Closing the handle closes its own descriptor. The kernel
lock releases after ALL descriptors for the same open file description close: a concurrent
fork can inherit a descriptor and prolong Busy until it closes or execs. Do not promise
unconditional immediate release merely because the original handle was dropped.
There is no Clone, mutable chain accessor, raw descriptor, PID authority, lock file or
stale-lock cleanup. Read-only inspection never creates, writes, repairs or mines;
OS atime effects are excluded. Writer ownership exposes no append or replacement yet.

The complete layout is manifest.v2 (exact public MNM2), blocks/ (contiguous 20-digit
height names ending .mrb2, each containing complete MRB2), and selection.v2 (MSS2).
Missing/extra selected entries, extra tails and caches reject. MSS2 has encoding
version 2, storage profile 1, generation 0 and exact length 232 bytes. Its fields are
C, genesis, height, tip, ledger_root, block count, manifest length, total block bytes,
SHA256d(exact MNM2), and SHA256d("MIRROR_STORAGE_SELECTION_V2" || first 200 record bytes).
Integers are little-endian; hashes retain raw byte order. Integrity checksums are not
authority. Other profiles or nonzero generations reject. Exact offsets, bounds and
error precedence are frozen in STORAGE_V2.md; do not silently reinterpret this format.

Before mutating files, initialization encodes the validated source. Under exclusive
ownership it syncs the existing parent; writes manifest and blocks with create_new
and sync_all; syncs blocks/root; writes and syncs selection.pending; renames it to
selection.v2 LAST; then syncs root. The stable root is never swapped. Preparation
failure before publication yields InitializationIncomplete. Once publication is attempted,
errors yield PublicationUncertain. Neither returns a store handle. Partial files remain
untouched. Root/ownership/layout prechecks may fail directly; an empty root may remain.
Reconciliation requires reopen against retained EXTERNAL selection. Pending markers
are never promoted automatically. Visible successful reopen cannot retroactively prove
a failed synchronization will survive another power loss. No append/reorg API exists.

Reopening bounds root enumeration, exact selection and manifest, every block length,
count and aggregate bytes before reading block payloads. Reads compare path/opened
file identity and take preflight length plus one sentinel. Static symlinks, nonregular
files and managed hardlinks reject. Complete MRB2 replays through ChainV2; persisted
ledger, population, approval or resource caches never become authority. An old valid
prefix rejects against later selected pins. Different membership branches reopen
independently and retain their own exact state; this is not durable reorganization.

PROFILE LIMITS AND FILESYSTEM TRUST
Profile 1 is Linux-only; other OSes return UnsupportedPlatform. Local tests exercised
Linux tmpfs and workspace overlayfs. Ubuntu CI verification is recorded above. WSL2's
Linux-native filesystem is intended but not directly tested here; native Windows,
DrvFS (/mnt/e), network and translated filesystems are not validated. The OS gate does
not certify mount types. Parent directories and local owners are trusted. All participants
must honor advisory locks; a locked root must not be renamed, replaced or removed.
Static inode/path checks are not race-free protection against hostile same-user path
replacement. Correct locks, atomic same-directory rename, and file/directory sync
are assumed. An error does not trigger a silently weaker fallback.

MNM2 is at most 2,781,636 bytes; MSS2 is exactly 232 bytes. Chain limits remain 4,096
blocks INCLUDING genesis and 16 MiB of complete MRB2. Maximum selected encoded payload
is 19,559,084 bytes; this is not a resident-memory limit. Chain replay also recomputes
the 1,048,576 cumulative state/configuration-item budget. Do not enlarge bounds, erase
history, prune permanent identities or restore counters from metadata to make recovery
fit. Generation-zero profile 1 is immutable; updates need reviewed versioning/migration.

